  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Thursday)\nIssued at 1151 AM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nNo change is expected to the overall pattern through Saturday. A couple of very small\nshowers could occur in the heat of each day near terrain, but the potential is below\nadding to the forecast. The large upper-level high pressure system now over the southern\nU.S. will evolve westward toward the weekend and tend to flatten some. This will allow\none or more weak disturbances aloft to brush the area on Sunday and/or Monday, which \ncould encourage a weak front or merged storm outflow boundaries into the area. If that\nhappens, the edge will come off the heat for some of us for a day or two and there\nwould be a bump in thunderstorm chances. But right now there is not a good signal in the \ndata for a real pattern shift. So a sustained general cool down is not expected through this\nforecast period. A Heat Advisory is in effect for tomorrow through Sunday. If dew points\ndo not drop a little in the next couple of days as expected, we will be near Heat Warning\ncriteria again in some areas.",
